adding a list of tasks to the context<pre><code># inside tasks/views.py

tasks = [
    {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "Listen to Music",
        "description": "Listen to some music",
        "due_date": "2026-12-12",
        "priority": "low",
        "created_at": "2026-10-07",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-07",
    },
    {
        "id": 2,
        "name": "Fix some bugs",
        "description": "Fix bugs in my code",
        "due_date": "2026-12-12",
        "priority": "high",
        "created_at": "2026-10-07",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-07",
    },
    {
        "id": 3,
        "name": "Fix some bugs",
        "description": "Fix bugs in my code",
        "due_date": "2026-12-12",
        "priority": "high",
        "created_at": "2026-10-07",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-07",
    },
]

def index(request):
    return render(request, "index.html", {"tasks": tasks})
</code></pre> <p>This introduces a dummy list of data which can look like actual database data for our tasks. Let us look at how we can display these in our template.</p> updated template with list of tasks<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;
    &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;Document&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;Tasks&lt;/h1&gt;
    {% for task in tasks %}
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;h2&gt;{{task.name}} &lt;small&gt;created on {{task.created_at}}&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;{{task.description}}&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    {% endfor %}

&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre> <p>By using the {% for %} tag, We have intrduced a <code>for</code> loop in our template to iterate on our <code>tasks</code> and display the same HTML for tasks that esist in our dummy data. </p> Displaying a list of data
